{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return a list of prime factors of the given integer, ordered from smallest to largest.\n    Each factor appears the correct number of times, and their product equals the input number.\n    \"\"\"\n    factors = []\n    d = 2\n    temp_n = n # Use a temporary variable for division\n\n    while d * d <= temp_n:\n        while temp_n % d == 0:\n            factors.append(d)\n            temp_n //= d\n        d += 1\n\n    if temp_n > 1:\n        factors.append(temp_n)\n    \n    return factors"}
