{"task_id": "HumanEval/31", "solution": "def is_prime(n):\n    \"\"\"Return true if a given number is prime, and false otherwise.\n    This function implements a standard primality test algorithm.\n    >>> is_prime(6)\n    False\n    >>> is_prime(101)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(11)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(13441)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(61)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(4)\n    False\n    >>> is_prime(1)\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    # Numbers less than 2 are not prime. This handles 1 and negative numbers.\n    if n < 2:\n        return False\n    # 2 is the only even prime number.\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    # All other even numbers are not prime.\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n    # Check for divisibility by odd numbers from 3 up to the square root of n.\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 2\n    return True"}
