{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "```python\ndef modp(n: int, p: int):\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p (be aware of numerics).\n    >>> modp(3, 5)\n    3\n    >>> modp(1101, 101)\n    2\n    >>> modp(0, 101)\n    1\n    >>> modp(3, 11)\n    8\n    >>> modp(100, 101)\n    1\n    \"\"\"\n    # According to business rules, 2^0 mod p is always 1.\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Compute 2^n mod p using Python's built-in modular exponentiation.\n    return pow(2, n, p)\n```"}
