{"task_id": "HumanEval/61", "solution": "```python\ndef correct_bracketing(brackets: str):\n    \"\"\" brackets is a string of \"(\" and \")\".\n    return True if every opening bracket has a corresponding closing bracket.\n\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"(\")\n    False\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"()\")\n    True\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"(()())\")\n    True\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\")(()\")\n    False\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"\")\n    True\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"((())\")\n    False\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"())\")\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    balance = 0\n    for char in brackets:\n        if char == '(':\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            balance -= 1\n        if balance < 0: # Early exit if a closing bracket appears without an open one.\n            return False\n    return balance == 0 # Final check to ensure all opening brackets are closed.\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/61", "solution": "```python\ndef correct_bracketing(brackets: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a string of brackets is properly matched and nested.\n    Returns True for valid sequences, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    counter = 0\n    for char in brackets:\n        if char == '(':\n            counter += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            counter -= 1\n        if counter < 0: # Detects an unmatched closing bracket.\n            return False\n    return counter == 0 # True if all opening brackets were matched.\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "def derivative(xs: list):\n    \"\"\" xs represent coefficients of a polynomial.\n    Returns the derivative of the polynomial.\n    \"\"\"\n    derivative_coeffs = []\n    # For each term xs[i] * x^i, its derivative is (xs[i] * i) * x^(i-1).\n    for i in range(1, len(xs)):\n        new_coeff = xs[i] * i\n        derivative_coeffs.append(new_coeff)\n    return derivative_coeffs"}
